  "title": "Document why the chat history uses feed and article",
  "body": "> Addresses #4471 and #4477\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\nNot required, development only.\n\n## Description\n\n`docs/ACCESSIBILITY.md` gave three short reasons for `role=\"feed\"` and `<article>` in the chat history, so the question in #4471 keeps coming back. This PR adds the structure as rendered today, the log/grid/feed comparison from #4471, why articles have no `aria-roledescription`, and what screen readers do with these roles.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `docs/ACCESSIBILITY.md`: expanded the \"Using `role=\"feed\"` and `role=\"article\"`\" section with \"Structure\", \"Why `feed` and not other roles\", \"Why not describe the article as a message\" and \"What screen readers do\"\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
